		{
			description: [
				"Magic Maps reveal major landmarks. Craft a Magic Map Focus, then the map, and explore methodically instead of wandering into locked biomes."
				"Craft and use the Magic Map to read major landmarks. Build a labelled portal lodge, mark cleared structures, and keep trophies because progression and later objectives may depend on proof of earlier victories."
				"Twilight Forest progression is advancement-gated. If an area inflicts a strange effect or blocks interaction, open the Twilight advancements and defeat the required earlier encounter rather than trying to bypass the biome."
				"Boss structures teach their own combat grammar through layout: hedge walls, tower stairs, swamp fire, maze levels, fortress doors, and frozen terrain are part of the encounter rather than scenery around it."
