		}
		{
			dependencies: ["667A4E8069400A5F"]
			description: [
				"Secure both sides of the portal, mark them clearly and store spare food, tools and blocks nearby. The safest portal is one a naked player can reach after a disaster."
				"Map boss arenas and completed structures rather than relying on memory. The forest repeats shapes and colours specifically to confuse careless travellers."
				"Bring trophies home for a shared hall, but leave signs at cleared sites so later explorers know what happened there."
				"Many structures contain unique blocks, plants, food, and materials beyond the boss reward. Survey after victory, take renewable samples, and preserve enough of the site that later players can understand what happened there."
			]
			id: "709157DA0DA51FE4"
			rewards: [{
				id: "798CE1711D885F72"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Every strange world needs a safe return"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0F548B57CACD057D"
				title: "I read and understood these field notes"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Build a Twilight Trailhead"
			x: 1.5d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Twilight Forest tracks progress through advancements and protects later biomes or dungeons. Strange weather, damage, blindness, locked blocks or green barrier particles usually mean a prerequisite is missing."
				"Open the Twilight Forest advancement page and trace the parent objective. Picking up trophies and boss drops can matter because possession often triggers the progression step."
				"Do not tunnel around protection or assume the region is broken. The warning is the dimension telling you which story branch to finish first."
				"Twilight Forest progression is advancement-gated. If an area inflicts a strange effect or blocks interaction, open the Twilight advancements and defeat the required earlier encounter rather than trying to bypass the biome."
			]
			id: "1FBEE5F24611BE52"
			rewards: [{
				id: "17B46B81488840DC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Acid rain, blindness and barriers are progression messages"
			tasks: [{
				id: "34102511C56844BE"
