				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Forest's Warning Effects"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1FBEE5F24611BE52"]
			description: [
				"Hedge Mazes, Hollow Hills, Quest Groves and several smaller structures can be explored without advancing the main bosses. They provide loot, creatures and breathing room between major dungeons."
				"Hollow Hills vary in size and danger. Hedge Mazes reward route marking. The Questing Ram asks for a collection rather than a fight."
				"Use side content to restock and learn the dimension, but do not confuse clearing it with unlocking a protected boss biome."
				"Boss structures teach their own combat grammar through layout: hedge walls, tower stairs, swamp fire, maze levels, fortress doors, and frozen terrain are part of the encounter rather than scenery around it."
			]
			id: "0BBE00E205F4C8A7"
			rewards: [{
				id: "44EA0F2C90DE06A0"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Not every landmark is part of the boss chain"
